<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Workspaces on Layer5 Documentation</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/</link><description>Recent content in Workspaces on Layer5 Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Manage Workspaces</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-workspaces/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-workspaces/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A workspace is the unit you use to organize designs and to decide which teams can reach an organization&amp;rsquo;s environments and connections. This guide covers every task on a workspace. For what a workspace is and how it relates to teams, environments, and designs, read the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/concepts/workspaces/"&gt;Workspaces concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each task names the permission it needs. Layer5 Cloud checks the permission in the organization that owns the workspace. A custom role or a team role can hold any of these permissions; the default holders are below.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Manage Environments</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-environments/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;An environment groups connections into a deploy target and is the means by which a workspace exposes those connections to its teams. This guide covers every task on an environment. For the model behind it, read the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1339/cloud/concepts/environments/"&gt;Environments concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each task names the permission it needs. Layer5 Cloud checks the permission in the organization that owns the environment.&lt;/p&gt;














